go 1.23

// The repo holds four Go modules that are released and consumed independently:
// one per protoc plugin, plus the conformance check that depends on
// grpc-gateway's own runtime.
//
// The workspace exists so a single command can build or test every module against
// the local sources rather than fetching each one from a proxy. Nothing here is
// required to build any single module: each directory still builds on its own
// with `go build ./...` and `GOWORK=off`.
use (
	./protoc-gen-grpc-gateway-typescript
	./protoc-gen-grpc-gateway-axios
	./protoc-gen-grpc-gateway-react-query

	// The conformance check is a separate module on purpose: it depends on
	// grpc-gateway's runtime and on Go types generated from the fixtures, and
	// those must never become dependencies of the plugins themselves.
	./protoc-gen-grpc-gateway-axios/conformance
)

// In workspace mode the build list is the union of every module's requirements, so
// a requirement pruned away in any single module still takes part here. That
// surfaces a long-standing ambiguity in genproto: the monolith module
// google.golang.org/genproto used to contain googleapis/api and googleapis/rpc
// before they were split out as separate modules, and grpc's opencensus
// dependency still requires an old monolith version. With both in the build list,
// the same import path resolves to two modules.
//
// Pinning the monolith to a version from after the split, where it no longer
// carries those directories, removes the ambiguity. This lives in the workspace
// rather than in any go.mod because it is a workspace-only consequence of the
// union, and each module builds correctly on its own without it.
replace google.golang.org/genproto => google.golang.org/genproto v0.0.0-20250102185135-69823020774d
